  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A professional roof inspection in Utah typically costs between $130 and $400, with most homeowners paying an average of $190\n.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $130 and $400"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The total price depends largely on the inspection method, roof size, and the type of documentation you require."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Inspection Type"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The method used to check your roof dictates the safety equipment and time required:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Basic Visual / Repair Estimates: Often Free. Many local contractors like Vertex Roofing SLC\nprovide a basic visual check at no cost if you use them for the subsequent repairs.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Vertex Roofing SLC",
                "link": "https://vertexroofingslc.com/roof-inspections/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Physical Walk-On Inspection: $75 to $200. The inspector climbs up to check shingles, flashing, and gutters by hand."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Drone Inspection\n: $150 to $450. Best for steep slopes, fragile materials, or hard-to-access roofs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Infrared / Thermal Imaging: $300 to $700. Uses specialized cameras to trace hidden leaks and moisture retention beneath the surface\n."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Pricing Factors in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Home Size: A standard 1,700-square-foot roof ranges from $125 to $357, while larger properties over 3,500 square feet can scale up to $735 according to .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://www.angi.com/articles/how-much-does-roof-inspection-cost.htm"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch & Stories: Multistory homes or steep rooflines common in snowy Utah mountain communities require more setup time and safety gear, adding $25 to $150 to the base price."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Reporting Needs: Formal written reports required for insurance claims, real estate transactions, or certifications typically cost an extra $75 to $200."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you would like to pinpoint a more accurate estimate for your property, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is the approximate square footage or number of stories of your home?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Are you experiencing an active\nleak or visible damage, or is this a routine check?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you need an informal assessment or a formal written report for insurance or a home sale?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
